{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792495015,"nonce":"3Y0ZV/yZUlSVmSFwvxUWvAaV0Kk=","title":"Composite scratch baking loses nested groups and path ranges","message":"Scoped follow-up to e0a7502e3e9d71bb983572df7db0033a67da1c48262e53368ae2399bc22e583a. Groups opened inside a composite scratch scope still write commands into the static batch and flatten alpha into each scratch child. render_subtree_to_layer_texture renders only primitive ranges and ignores commands and tessellated paths. Overlapping children therefore fade independently. Promoted root animation opacity must remain on the final blit, with only nested/base groups baked.\n\nCoordinate scratch command ownership, balanced saved-owner Pops, local counts, ordered tight baking with straight-alpha output, cache invalidation for command/effect/path changes, and a full-repaint fallback for CSS records whose indices belong to scratch. Add offscreen overlap/path/cache and actual promoted-walker regressions. Keep foreground/late-image and cross-stream ancestor isolation in the parent. No pushes authorized.","files":null}]}